<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

However, to correctly reflect the condition that the vector contains exactly the same elements in the same order as the collection `c`, we need to ensure that the sizes match and the elements are equal. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
